0 1 0 0 0 0 2 1\n0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 2 0\n0 0 0 0 0 2 0 0 2 0\n0 0 2 0 0 2 0 0 2 0\n0 0 2 0 2 2 0 0 2 0\n0 0 2 0 2 2 2 0 2 0\n\nYour final answer should just be the python script itself, no other text or markdown.",
  "raw_response": "```python\ndef solve(grid):\n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0])\n    result = [row[:] for row in grid]\n    \n    for c in range(cols):\n        # Find 2s in this column\n        twos = [r for r in range(rows) if grid[r][c] == 2]\n        if not twos:\n            continue\n        count = len(twos)\n        # Remove 2s\n        for r in twos:\n            result[r][c] = 0\n        # Find the topmost 2 position, then slide up from there into 0s\n        top2 = twos[0]\n        # Move upward from top2-1 while it's 0, to find where to place\n        pos = top2\n        while pos > 0 and result[pos-1][c] == 0:\n            pos -= 1\n        # Place count 2s starting at pos going down\n        for i in range(count):\n            result[pos + i][c] = 2\n    \n    return result\n```",
  "script": "def solve(grid):\n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0])\n    result = [row[:] for row in grid]\n    \n    for c in range(cols):\n        # Find 2s in this column\n        twos = [r for r in range(rows) if grid[r][c] == 2]\n        if not twos:\n            continue\n        count = len(twos)\n        # Remove 2s\n        for r in twos:\n            result[r][c] = 0\n        # Find the topmost 2 position, then slide up from there into 0s\n        top2 = twos[0]\n        # Move upward from top2-1 while it's 0, to find where to place\n        pos = top2\n        while pos > 0 and result[pos-1][c] == 0:\n            pos -= 1\n        # Place count 2s starting at pos going down\n        for i in range(count):\n            result[pos + i][c] = 2\n    \n    return result",
